    "sourceNumber": 18,
    "topic": "Circuits & Current",
    "html": "<P>\r\n<TABLE style=\"border-spacing:1px;padding:1px;border:none;width:7.5in\">\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD COLSPAN=\"3\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;font-weight: bold;\">MULTIPLE CHOICE.  Choose the one alternative that best completes the statement or answers the question.</span>\r\n</TD>\r\n</TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD COLSPAN=\"3\">\r\n&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n</TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD ALIGN=\"RIGHT\" style=\"vertical-align:top;width:0.5in\">\r\n18)&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n<TD style=\"width:6.0in\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;\">If a quantity you calculated has units of <img src=\"images/f1q18g1.jpg\" alt=\"(kg &#8729; m2/s2 &#8729; C)\" style=\"vertical-align: -20.0px;\" />, what is that quantity?</span>\r\n</TD><TD style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1.0in\">\r\n18)&nbsp;______\r\n</TD></TR></TABLE>\r\n<TABLE style=\"border-spacing:1px;padding:1px;border:none\">\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD style=\"width:0.75in\">\r\n&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n<TD>\r\nA)&nbsp;\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;\">potential difference</span>\r\n</TD>\r\n</TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD style=\"width:0.75in\">\r\n&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n<TD>\r\nB)&nbsp;\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;\">capacitance</span>\r\n</TD>\r\n</TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD style=\"width:0.75in\">\r\n&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n<TD>\r\nC)&nbsp;\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;\">charge</span>\r\n</TD>\r\n</TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD style=\"width:0.75in\">\r\n&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n<TD>\r\nD)&nbsp;\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;\">resistivity</span>\r\n</TD>\r\n</TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD style=\"width:0.75in\">\r\n&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n<TD>\r\nE)&nbsp;\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;\">resistance</span>\r\n</TD>\r\n</TR>\r\n</TABLE>\r\n</P>"
