    "sourceNumber": 51,
    "topic": "Magnetism",
    "html": "<P>\r\n<TABLE style=\"border-spacing:1px;padding:1px;border:none;width:7.5in\">\r\n<TR><TD COLSPAN=\"3\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Times New Roman;font-size: 10pt;\"><img src=\"images/f1q51g1.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"vertical-align: 0.0px;\" height=\"105\" width=\"291\" /></span>\r\n</TD></TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD ALIGN=\"RIGHT\" style=\"vertical-align:top;width:0.5in\">\r\n51)&nbsp;\r\n</TD>\r\n<TD style=\"width:6.0in\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family: Palatino Linotype;font-size: 10pt;\">Locations 1 and 2 are next to parallel wires that have constant currents <span style=\"font-style: italic;\">I</span> and 2<span style=\"font-style: italic;\">I</span> flowing through them in the same direction. The wires are separated by distance <span style=\"font-style: italic;\">d</span>, and oriented so that the current is flowing into the page, as shown by the cross-sectional diagram above. Locations 1 and 2 are in the plane of the wires, at distances <span style=\"font-style: italic;\">d </span>and 2<span style=\"font-style: italic;\">d </span>from the two wires, as shown. Which of the following correctly show the direction of the magnetic field at locations 1 and 2? Select two answers&#8211;one from each column.<br /><br /></span><span style=\"font-family: Times New Roman;font-size: 10pt;\"><img src=\"images/f1q51g2.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"vertical-align: 0.0px;\" height=\"310\" width=\"325\" /></span>\r\n</TD><TD style=\"vertical-align:top;width:1.0in\">\r\n51)&nbsp;______\r\n</TD></TR></TABLE>\r\n</P>"
